WEBVTT

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.540
The Worst Day of Masaru's Life!

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.540
Soulmon the Prankster!

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.270
The Worst Day of Masaru's Life!

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:08.460
Soulmon the Prankster!

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.710
Hey, Masaru-niichan...

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.180
Is this really where Tohma-kun lives?

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.660
It's an incredible mansion!

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.020
It's like a castle.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.150
Don't look at me.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.650
This is my first time coming here, too.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.520
I think I'll go back home.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.050
You're the one who said you promised to come here.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.240
But I didn't think you would come with me!

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.830
I thought you'd feel discouraged if you came here alone, so I took the time to...

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.410
That doesn't matter!

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.120
Just forget it, I'm going home!

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.420
Daimon Masaru-sama, Chika-sama, and Agumon-sama.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.490
Tohma-sama is waiting for you.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.760
Please come in.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.250
S-Sure.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.690
Wow.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.900
There's no need to take off your shoes.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:16.110
S-Sorry!

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.790
Welcome, Chika-chan and big brother!

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:25.170
Who are you calling your big brother?

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:28.750
Thank you for inviting us!

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.780
This stuff is amazing...

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.500
How much did this cost?

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.890
Masaru-niichan!

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:49.050
I enjoyed your hospitality the other day, so please accept this modest meal as my thanks.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:51.790
Whoa, this looks pretty good!

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:53.040
Masaru-niichan!

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.680
Don't you have any fried eggs?

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.320
I can get them to make some if you'd like.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.290
Agu-chan, you're embarrassing me too...

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.960
What's wrong, Chika-chan?

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:10.960
Well...

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.250
Don't hold yourself back.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:13.850
Go on.

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.020
O-Okay!

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.130
Hey, drink water! Water!

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:30.710
That water is used to wash your fingertips!

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.150
Are you okay, Chika-chan?

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.390
Gaomon!

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.410
Yes, Master.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.330
Delicious! This water's just what you'd expect coming from Tohma's place!

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.190
Chika, you should drink some, too!

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:49.370
Stop it!

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.750
Stupid Masaru-niichan!

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.980
I mean, what's your problem?!

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.790
Masaru-niichan...

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.040
Masaru-niichan...

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.790
I hope you slip on the street and hit your head, run into a signpost, fall off a bridge...

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.730
get run over by a car...

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.860
and get squashed by a tanker!

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.030
Hey, Chika!

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:24.780
Chika-chan!

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:29.520
Chika!

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:30.700
Aniki!

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.040
A banana?

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:53.080
What's a banana peel doing here?

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:55.190
Hey! Hey!

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:58.330
What was all that she said about slipping and hitting my head, anyway?

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.350
Aniki!

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.010
Aniki, listen to me!

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.110
Slipping and hitting my head...?

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.110
Ah, geez!

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:02.330
Aniki!

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:03.480
There's a Digimon here!

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:06.220
Masaru...

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.010
Is there something wrong with Gaomon?

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.740
That's not what I meant!

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.500
There's a Digimon right next to you!

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:13.970
Huh?

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:15.840
No there isn't.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:18.440
Behind you! Behind you!

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.580
Geez!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.300
Aniki, hold still!

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.270
I'll get that bastard off you!

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.380
What are you doing?!

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.340
That hurt!

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.320
H-Huh?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:32.680
Take that!

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.580
But...!

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:33.790
And that!

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.800
Gaomon, you can see it, right?

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.000
The Digimon that's stuck itself onto Aniki!

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:43.120
Digimon?

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:43.800
What are you talking about?

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:46.210
You can't see it?!

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.050
Well, look at that.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:51.200
Anyway, is it all right to let Chika-chan run off like that?

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:53.380
Crap!

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.770
The problem is...

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:59.140
you're too thick-headed when it comes to other people's feelings.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:00.140
Thick-headed?

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:01.250
What part of me?

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.690
My point exactly.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:08.700
I can understand perfectly how Chika-chan must've felt when she said that parting shot at you.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.770
By "parting shot" you mean...

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.160
All that stuff she said about slipping and getting hit?

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:14.710
Yeah.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:16.660
Slipping on the street and hitting your head...

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.580
then running into a signpost, I believe.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.280
A signpost, huh?

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:26.740
Aniki, Aniki!

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.670
I feel a Digimon close by again!

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.160
Again?

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.530
Oww!

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:39.100
What's a signpost doing over here?!

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.060
I told you, a Digimon is doing this!

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.020
That's odd.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:45.460
Yeah, it is!

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.930
There's gotta be something wrong with you, Agumon!

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:48.870
Not that.

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:55.990
From the looks of that signpost, it seems
 as though Chika-chan used some sort of magic to put a curse on you.

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:57.950
A curse?

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.570
Everything is going exactly as Chika-chan had said.

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:03.210
First, you slipped on the street and nearly hit yourself...

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:04.920
And now, you've run into a signpost.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:07.380
That's not possible!

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.460
The next one was falling from a bridge, right, Master?

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:11.460
Gaomon.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.990
That'll never happen!

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:17.850
I mean, there aren't even any bridges near here!

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.230
Oww!

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:24.160
I'm sorry!

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:26.180
I am so sorry, are you okay?

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.830
What the hell?!

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:27.570
I'm sorry!

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.570
NOTE: <i>Hashi</i> (はし) can mean both a bridge (橋) and chopsticks (箸).

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.570
He fell... from chopsticks...

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.190
Oww...

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:35.580
I'm not gonna believe in this curse business!

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.120
Man, that hurt...

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:44.900
What's going on?!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.210
We have a Digimon signal.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.410
What? Where?

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:50.990
It's coming from inside DATS headquarters!

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:54.550
In other words, right here... but...

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:58.460
It's Aniki!

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:00.680
The Digimon signal is coming from Aniki!

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:01.850
Huh?

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.640
Wait, what do you mean by that?

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.310
Daimon Masaru.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.610
You are put under restraint.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.390
Are you saying I purposely brought it along?

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:14.490
It's possible.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:15.260
Very possible.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.880
This is you we're talking about, Masaru.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:17.710
Huh?!

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.130
Everyone, listen to me, please!

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:23.710
There's a Digimon attached to Aniki right now!

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.560
Attached?

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.870
It turned invisible and hovered next to him!

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:32.870
Then it left stuff like the banana peel and signpost in his path, hurting him...

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.040
Aniki is the victim!

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:37.030
Then...

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:41.280
All those little accidents that I was certain were due to his blockheadedness...

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:43.310
were all acts of a Digimon?

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:45.810
Don't call me a blockhead!

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.270
That should be the least of your worries.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:53.280
Our main problem here is that a Digimon was allowed forbidden entry into DATS headquarters.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.990
A Digimon that was urged from Chika-chan's words...

00:08:56.990 --> 00:09:01.660
is turning those harmless thoughts of hers into reality.

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:04.870
What were the rest?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:06.470
Captain!

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:10.340
The words that haven't been transformed into reality yet... what were the rest of them?

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:16.440
Slipping on the street and hitting his head, running into a signpost, falling from a bridge...

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:20.550
Pursued by a car, and run over by a tanker, Captain.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.300
Cut the crap!

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:26.540
I can't stand listening anymore! You're making this sound like it's Chika's fault!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.810
You guys know Chika would never use a Digimon!

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:33.640
Hey, you! The Digimon clinging onto me!

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.150
Come on out! You're playing dirty!

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.770
How dare you turn invisible and attack behind my back...!

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.360
Oh!

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:44.520
Chika...

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.540
I just have to find Chika, right?

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:52.750
Then you'll see that she has nothing to do with that Digimon!

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:06.660
He was just... chased by a car... I think...

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:09.250
NOTE: <i>Kuruma</i> (くるま) can mean either a car or a vehicle.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.250
Then all that's left is being run over by a tanker.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.370
Oh, c'mon. A tanker?

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:12.620
That's impossible.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:15.520
It would make sense if we were on water, but we're on the shore now.

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.340
What now?

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:37.360
A 20 kiloton tanker named the A.L. has lost control.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.540
The Maritime Safety Agency has sent an SOS!

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:42.940
It's moving at 23 knots!

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:46.600
In 10 minutes and 35 seconds, it will hit DATS headquarters!

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.310
Our maximum priority...

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.360
is to ensure the safety of the tanker's crew!

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.600
The MSA has sent a helicopter to them...

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.940
but it's uncertain whether or not it can get there in 10 minutes...

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:04.490
I'll take all of the barriers we're using in our base and rebuild them to prepare for the collision!

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:05.990
Wait a minute!

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.800
The tanker's coming after me, right?

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.960
So I'll have to meet it face on!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.370
What are you thinking?

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:14.500
Clearly...

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.920
this is a one-on-one fight between me and the tanker!

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:18.880
Don't be stupid!

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:21.300
I just have to get out there!

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:22.590
If it's a fight it wants, I accept!

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:25.340
This isn't the time for jokes!

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.560
Going against a tanker is impossible!

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:28.780
She's right.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.430
Right now, we should be...

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:36.020
Don't get in my way. All you have to do is watch.

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:37.860
Don't tell me...

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:39.030
Masaru, are you...?

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:40.230
Shut up!

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:41.570
Don't follow me!

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:43.490
Aniki!

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:46.660
Wait for me, Aniki!

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:51.870
He is such an idiot.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:53.620
He sure is.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:56.040
It seems he has a problem expressing himself.

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:01.870
Because he didn't want DATS to suffer damage,

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:04.010
he purposely left to get far away from here.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.510
He's quite an obvious fellow.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.070
There's only 10 minutes left.

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:12.960
We must find something, anything, that'll resolve this.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.040
Of course.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:14.640
Yeah.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:19.020
You guys...!

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:21.690
Okay! I'll do something, too!

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:27.620
Chika! Chika!!

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:30.840
Agu-chan?

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:33.020
W-Wai-...!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:36.560
What are you doing here?! What if someone sees you?!

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.880
Aniki's in trouble because of you!

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:41.840
I don't care about Masaru-niichan.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:45.920
You're the only one who can help him, Chika!

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.440
Why me?!

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:49.790
Because he's gonna get run over by a tanker!

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.240
A tanker? That's ridiculous.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:53.290
And I don't care.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.410
Of course you care!

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:57.590
Aniki might die!

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:58.930
And I said, I don't care.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:12:59.740
Don't say that!

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:01.830
It's because you said all those weird things to him...!

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:03.160
They're not weird!

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.400
Anyway, why do I have to take responsibility?!

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:06.460
I don't care!

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:07.640
The Digimon!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.390
It's the Digimon's fault!

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:13.020
Masaru-niichan can take care of himself against that!

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:13.880
He is!

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:16.620
But it's no good unless you help him!

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:17.580
He's an idiot.

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:19.940
No, he's not!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:20.950
Then what?

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:23.110
Er, Aniki is Aniki...

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:23.910
You're an idiot.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:25.590
No, you're the idiot!

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:29.370
Look at that!

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.750
Aniki turned himself into the bait to lure it away from hurting other people!

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.570
He's really gonna get hit by that tanker!

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.380
Masaru-niichan!

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:50.160
According to the information gathered and the Digimon signal left at the crime scene...

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:52.240
we were able to narrow down the specific Digimon.

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:56.700
Soulmon

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:56.700
Adult Level

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:56.700
Soulmon. He's an Adult Level, Ghost-type Digimon.

00:13:57.550 --> 00:14:04.300
Because he's small and he can instantly turn himself invisible, we were unable to track him through our Digimon radars.

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:07.260
This is worrisome.

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:11.640
If we could at least see his form, we could knock him flat with one hit...

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:12.530
Yoshino.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:15.460
You're becoming more and more like Masaru these days.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.460
What part?

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:20.960
What's wrong, Tohma?

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.690
Soulmon. An invisible enemy.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:25.560
Do you have any plans against him?

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:26.400
If it's possible...

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.780
I wasn't serious when I said that!

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:37.590
Masaru-niichan was embarrassing me, and it made me mad...

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:39.540
I just said it because I was angry!

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:42.380
Aniki isn't embarrassing!

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:44.000
He's strong and awesome!

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:46.000
I know that!

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:49.620
Masaru-niichan!

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:50.680
Chika!

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.900
Masaru-niichan!

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:54.890
No! Run!

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:56.780
Get away!!

00:14:58.690 --> 00:14:59.270
Chika-chan.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.040
He can't do that.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:04.820
That's the sort of person he is.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.730
I'm sure you understand that well enough.

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.980
But... if he doesn't...

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:14.240
It'll be okay. He won't get crushed by that tanker.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:15.940
That'll never happen.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:16.870
I won't let it.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:27.800
Bring it on!

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:29.310
You're a moron.

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.470
Tohma! Chika! Wh-What are you doing here?

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:36.440
This is why people who don't think logically get on my nerves.

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:37.800
What?!

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:38.930
Listen carefully, Chika-chan.

00:15:39.650 --> 00:15:42.980
Soulmon isn't using magic.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:47.150
You can't move or erase something just by chanting a spell.

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:53.050
That Digimon only has the special power of invisibility.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.140
I get it.

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:57.800
Since we can't see the Digimon, he uses that to his advantage to pull pranks.

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:58.980
Correct.

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:02.740
So the banana peel and signpost and stuff were also because of a Digimon...

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:04.420
Then, that tanker must be the same!

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.450
Masaru! Tohma!

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:12.920
Yoshino!

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:17.060
The ship's captain contacted us, saying he can't get near the rudder.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:18.890
Something keeps blocking his way.

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.200
Just as I'd presumed.

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:23.800
The Digimon went into the tanker and took over the helm.

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:24.540
Let's get...

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:25.850
Wait, where do you think you're going?

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.610
To secure the Digimon, of course.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:31.250
I told you already: This is my fight!

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:32.070
Don't interfere.

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:33.470
I'm coming, too!

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:34.660
Masaru-niichan!

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:41.820
Don't worry, Chika!

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.710
I'll beat him up for you, too!

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:45.620
Fine, I got it.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:47.860
Masaru, catch.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:49.690
Whoa!

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:51.540
Use that.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:52.880
Huh? What is it?

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:55.840
A little magic known as science.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:57.550
Huh?

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:58.650
Here we go!

00:16:58.650 --> 00:16:59.780
Grab on!

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.120
Hold the wheel.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.510
Let's go, Agumon!

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.070
Yeah!

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.840
Its distance has reached 500!

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:25.150
All branches have taken refuge!

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:26.710
You two should also get out of here.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:28.040
Captain!

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:36.920
The control room is...

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:38.010
Over there!

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:40.700
We're getting revenge for frightening Chika!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:41.770
Let's go, Agumon!

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:42.470
Yeah!

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:53.850
We can't see him...

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:55.550
but that doesn't mean his body doesn't exist.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:56.240
Yeah.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:56.990
So that means...

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:01.410
You're in here holding that rudder!

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:03.700
You bastard!

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:06.190
Are you here? Here? Here?!

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:08.410
We know you're in here, bastard!

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:09.210
Stop!

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:12.240
He can see us, but we can't see him.

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.420
That makes it easy for him to run away!

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:16.880
But... what if I used this?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.260
That spray...

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:24.600
is made up of special particles that react to the substance that Digimon are made up of.

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:31.030
There you are!

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:33.060
How dare you make a fool outta me!

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:35.250
Now I'm gonna get my payback!

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.420
This one's for Chika!

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.290
Damn, he got bigger! {huhuhu}

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:51.310
Aniki!

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:51.750
Yeah!

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:57.270
Digisoul Charge!

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:03.390
Agumon, evolve!

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:14.920
<b>mou nani mo nai sekai ja kandou dekinai</b>

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:14.920
<b>A world that's full of nothing can't inspire anyone</b>

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:15.430
GeoGreymon!

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:19.880
<b>sou, kizuita sono hi kara wakaru no sa</b>

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:19.880
<b>You'll understand what I mean after the day you realize that</b>

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.990
<b>furue wo tomete</b>

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.990
<b>Stop your trembling</b>

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:25.610
<b>hitomi wo hirake</b>

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:25.610
<b>Open your eyes</b>

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:30.420
<b>kimi no jikan wo tokihanate!</b>

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:30.420
<b>And liberate your time!</b>

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:34.620
<b>mirai e Shootin' star!</b>

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:34.620
<b>Oh shootin' star to the future!</b>

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:37.910
<b>hikari no aachi egake</b>

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:37.910
<b>Draw an arch of light</b>

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:43.180
<b>todoku no sa shinjitsuzukeru naraba</b>

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:43.180
<b>As long as you keep believing, it'll reach up there</b>

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:48.980
<b>kimi wo yobu koe ga kokoro de hajiketara</b>

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:48.980
<b>When the voice that calls you bellows with the heart</b>

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:45.680
Mega Burst!

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:55.150
<b>subete ga hajimaru Believer!</b>

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:55.150
<b>That's when everything will begin, Believer!</b>

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.560
You did it!

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:04.500
It stopped.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:15.300
Masaru-niichan!

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:17.590
Thanks, Chika.

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:21.550
Because of your help...

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:22.220
Look!

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:24.420
That's right!

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:25.670
You'd better be grateful!

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:27.230
Hey, what about me?

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:29.030
Oh yeah, you helped too, Agumon!

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:29.620
Hey!

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:35.660
You look grim.

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:36.480
Captain.

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:43.150
Have you ever wondered why that Digimon carried out each of Chika-chan's wishes?

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:51.540
Why do Digimon come into the human world? And why do Digimon commit crimes?

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:56.410
Perhaps it has something to do with people's thoughts.

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:58.270
Thoughts? You mean their emotions?

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.850
Yes, sir.

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:04.190
A few days ago, in the incidents involving Hanamura Neon and Hayase-senshu...

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:07.260
Both of them had strong desires and volition,

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:10.060
which their corresponding Digimon's actions were closely involved in.

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:15.900
Are Digimon acting upon the human's effect on them?

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:19.490
Or are humans affected by the Digimon?

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:24.800
In either case, I believe that we should act as urgently as possible to unravel the secrets of that relationship.

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:27.190
The relationship between Digimons and humans, huh?

